* The Gram argument of two indices ` A ` , ` B ` of a parity system with the selected zeros ` H A ` , ` H B ` (Lean ` gramArg_re_bounds ` , ` gramArg_height ` , ` gramArg_im ` ): the character ` chi_A chi_B ^ -1 ` is in the group and is principal exactly when ` chi_B = chi_A ` ; ` s = ( H A - S ) + conj ( H B - S ) ` has ` 0 <_ Re s <_ 1 / 50 ` , ` Im s = Im H A - Im H B ` and ` N ( abs Im s + 2 ) <_ 2 N ( T + 2 ) ` .

